name: Link Analysis procurement fraud showcase
tagline: "A seeded bid-rigging and procurement fraud Link Analysis demo - bid rotation, cover bids, a conflict of interest and a phoenix firm, planted among 1 200 tenders and 6 000 bids with benign look-alikes"
description: "The bid-rigging and procurement fraud Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Seven synthetic feeds (company, director, procurement_person, official, tender, bid, contract_change; tenders published over 12 months from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, the next month in data/staged; 900 companies, 2 000 people of whom 300 are buying officials, about 1 230 tenders, 6 000 bids and 800 contract changes) are landed by seven Collectors and Pipelines. The procurement_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via, market) of seven link kinds; two derived Jobs build the Datasets behind the approvals and debarment views. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-procurement-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by ProcurementLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-procurement-data.test.mjs): four road firms win Highways North's 24 road tenders in turn, losing bids 5-12 % above the winner, two of them sharing a director; three IT competitors cover-bid for one winner, 60 % of their bids from its IP address within minutes and most with its estimator as author; a Parks official approves 9 contract changes for a grounds firm whose director lives at the official's address; a debarred cleaning firm's directors run a new firm that wins within 3 months. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: three large road firms that win often but bid independently, the buyer's public help-desk kiosk shared by 14 small firms, a Facilities contracts manager approving many changes across unrelated suppliers, and a director who joins an unrelated firm years after a debarment. Four saved views. Basic tier: runs on every edition, Basic included. Advanced tier, in the same template and inert on Basic: Demo Users and roles (config/demo-users.toon, roles.toon: procurement.analyst lead, procurement.manager second approver, procurement.reviewer read-only, procurement.outsider not a member, admin), four-eyes above a fan-out of 2000 and Drafts (link-analysis.toon), the procurement_shared_ip_counts and procurement_shared_ip_alerts Jobs and the Alert Rule procurement_same_tender_shared_ip, a bid from an IP address already used by another bidder on the same tender (on the shipped data it counts 16 bids on 8 tenders, every one a cover bid from the winning IT firm's office address, never the help-desk kiosk, from which no two firms ever bid on one tender; unarmed on Basic). Investigations, members, an Entity List, a Case, a held four-eyes expand and a Draft are runtime state: run `node tools/seed-la-procurement.mjs --apply` on an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth. Synthetic data only."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:building-library
contents[7]: "7 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "procurement_links Job + Dataset (7 link kinds, via, market) and 2 derived view Datasets", "4 saved views (bid rotation, cover bids, change approvals, debarred firms' directors)", "4 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Ground truth and golden tests in the repository", "Advanced tier: 5 Demo Users + role table, four-eyes (inert on Basic)", "Advanced tier: Alert Rule on a bid from an IP address another bidder already used on the same tender (counts Job + evaluate Job, unarmed on Basic)"
